---@class CisZone
-- A zone as this library holds it, after defaults are applied. A caller never constructs one; it is what CreateZone made out of a name, a shape and CisZoneOptions.
---@field name string the name the caller gave it, and the handle remove takes
---@field kind string 'box', 'poly' or 'sphere'
---@field owner string the resource that created it. Taken from the invoking resource, never from an argument, so two resources can both use "door1"
---@field debug boolean whether a draw thread is running for it
local CisZone = {}

---@class CisZoneDebug
-- The live debug record GetZoneDebug answers -- not a copy. insideCount and insideNames are rebuilt on every pass and zeroed when the last zone goes.
---@field lastPassMs? number how long the last grid pass took
---@field lastPassAt? integer GetGameTimer at the end of the last pass
---@field debugDrawing? boolean whether a draw thread is running right now
---@field insideCount? integer the zones the library believes the player is in
---@field insideNames? string[] their names, sorted
local CisZoneDebug = {}

---@class CisZoneOptions
-- The options table for Cis.zones.* and Cis.target.add. Every field is optional; a zone is created with defaults when one is absent. From init.lua (Cis.zones.*) the function fields are plain local functions run in the calling resource; through the CreateZone export they arrive as funcrefs. The event-name twins fire either way.
---@field onEnter? fun(zone: CisZone, coords: vector3) called pcall'd on the inside edge, with the ZONE and the player's own coordinates
---@field onExit? fun(zone: CisZone, coords: vector3) called pcall'd on the outside edge and on removal
---@field inside? fun(zone: CisZone) called every insideInterval while the player is inside
---@field insideInterval? integer ms between inside calls, default 500. Clamped up to 250 whenever insideEvent is set, so a networked event cannot be asked for faster than a quarter second
---@field debug? boolean truthy starts the draw thread once registration succeeds
---@field onEnterEvent? string fires with (zoneName, x, y, z). Falls back to TriggerServerEvent when onEnter is absent. Every event name is a string of 1 to 128 bytes; anything else refuses the zone by name
---@field onExitEvent? string fires with (zoneName, x, y, z). The only way a consumer outside this VM learns the player left
---@field insideEvent? string its presence is what forces the 250ms clamp
---@field local? boolean exactly true switches ALL THREE events (onEnterEvent, onExitEvent, insideEvent) to client-local TriggerEvent instead of TriggerServerEvent. A local event from a resource other than cis_libs must be named <resource>:... -- the creating resource -- so it cannot fire cis_libs:cache, onResourceStop or the events of another resource with cis_libs as the invoker
---@field minZ? number the floor, default -1000.0, and the fallback Z for any poly point with no z. Must be finite and no higher than maxZ
---@field maxZ? number the ceiling, default 10000.0
---@field thickness? number poly only: a slab this many metres tall around the average z of the points, as ox_lib; ignored when minZ or maxZ is given
---@field heading? number the box heading; a finite number
---@field rotation? number an alias for the box heading
local CisZoneOptions = {}

