---@overload fun(...)
  ---@param name string #a non-empty handler name, the key everything else is filed under
  ---@param handler function|string|table #a function, a callable reference table (a function passed from another resource; released when that resource stops), or a "resource:Export" string; nil fails all three. A later registration of the same name by the SAME resource replaces the earlier one, whatever its kind; a name another resource holds is refused (cis_libs may replace any)
  ---@param opts? table #{ remote = true|false, ace = 'object', schema = { field = { type, min, max, maxLen, optional, finite } }, maxStringLen = n }. remote defaults to TRUE (1.0.0 behaviour); remote = false makes the callback unreachable from any client, which is answered 'unknown' exactly as for a missing name. ace is checked with IsPrincipalAceAllowed('player.<src>', ace) and refused 'denied'. schema checks the FIRST argument and refuses 'bad payload' (and reports the player); its rules are the same as SecureNetOn's, so type may be integer and infinity is refused unless finite = false. maxStringLen replaces the default string cap (Config.CallbackLimits.MaxStringLen, 4096) for this callback; every remote call is capped, keys and values. A malformed option is refused, never ignored
  ---@return boolean, string|nil #true once bound; false plus the reason (also logged) on a refusal
---@overload
  ---@param name string #a non-empty handler name; a non-string or "" is refused before anything is stored, and so is a name another resource holds (the owner may replace its own; a name is free again once its owner stops)
  ---@param fn function|string #a callable, or a "resource:Export" string
  ---@return boolean, string|nil #true once stored; false plus the reason (also logged) on a refusal
---@overload
function RegisterCallback.server(name, handler, opts) end
function RegisterCallback.client(name, fn) end

---@overload fun(...)
  ---@param slot string #a CisRegistry.SLOTS key; an unknown slot is refused before dispatch
  ---@param provider string #always "resource:Export" -- a function cannot cross the exports boundary and arrives as nil
  ---@param contract? string #the caller's declared contract, normally the engine's own reading of its fxmanifest cis_libs_contract. A MAJOR mismatch is refused before dispatch, because a 3.x product registering into a 2.x cis_libs gets calls that return the wrong value for the right reason
  ---@return boolean, string #true on registration; false plus a reason on a major contract mismatch, a caller off Security.AuthorizedResources, or a refusal
---@overload
  ---@param slot string #a CisRegistry.SLOTS key; an unknown slot is refused before dispatch
  ---@param provider string|table|function #a "resource:Export" string, a table carrying .resource, or a bare callable
  ---@param contract? string #as on the server: a MAJOR mismatch is refused before dispatch
  ---@return boolean, string|nil #true, or false plus a reason naming the slot, the holder, or a caller off the server's allow-list. Before the server's allow-list reaches the client a foreign registration is held: true plus 'held until the server sends the allow-list', then filed or refused (and logged) when it arrives
---@overload
function RegisterCapability.server(slot, provider, contract) end
function RegisterCapability.client(slot, provider, contract) end

