---@param opts? table #windowMs, maxHits, the payload bounds maxArgs, maxStringLen, maxEntries and maxDepth (32, 4096, 256 and 8 by default), and optional schema. schema is a map of field -> { type, min, max, maxLen, optional, finite } on the first payload table; type may be integer, and infinity is refused unless finite = false. An oversized or bad payload is refused, counted as netSchemaRefused, and reported through Cis.security.report, once per run of them
---@return boolean, string #true once registered, false plus a reason when it is refused -- so a refusal is visible rather than indistinguishable from success
